# Velnora frontend does not currently require any environment variables.
# This file exists to establish the convention for when one is needed.
#
# Reminder: anything exposed through a Vite client-side variable (any name
# prefixed VITE_) is bundled into the JavaScript shipped to every visitor's
# browser. It is PUBLIC, not a secret, no matter how it's named.
#
#   VITE_SOME_PUBLIC_CONFIG=example-value
#
# Real secrets (API keys, database URLs, JWT signing secrets, third-party
# service credentials, etc.) must live on a server/backend that the browser
# never sees, not in this file, not with a VITE_ prefix, and not committed
# to git. See SECURITY.md for details.
